    <div class="col"><h3>Reading the ranges</h3>The low–high model range is the practical planning band. Each model's own 80% interval for the 2027 total (in <i>forecast_annual.csv</i>) ranges from ±{{ n.pi_halfwidth["Prophet"] | pct(0, False) }} for Prophet to ±{{ n.pi_halfwidth["Holt-Winters"] | pct(0, False) }} for Holt-Winters. They disagree too much, and Prophet's is far tighter than its back-test misses, so we don't headline them.</div>
    <div class="col"><h3>Reproduce</h3><i>python src/backtest.py</i> → <i>python src/prophet_sensitivity.py</i> → <i>python src/forecast_2027.py</i> → <i>python report/build_report.py</i>. Data refresh: <i>data/sql/extract_parakeet_daily.sql</i> via MCP Andersons.</div>
